      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "Factor G as BᵀB. The box pulled back by B has volume 4ᵈ, greater than the Minkowski threshold 2ᵈ. The nonzero lattice vector inside gives ℓᵈ≤(4d)ᵈ det G. Applying this to G and G⁻¹ under the contrary assumption and multiplying gives 2ᵈ≤1. Smith normal form supplies a first primitive basis vector dividing the resulting short vector.",
      "review": "Checked the strict volume threshold, positivity of d, the cancellation of the two determinants and division by a nonzero integer whose square is at least one."
