    {
      "id": "LTR-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The Schur complement lifts a covering bound through one coordinate",
      "anchor": "inputs-transference-round",
      "statement": "In real dimension d≥0 one may choose C₀=1, C_d=C_(d−1)+8d². A dual squared lower bound δ>0 implies that every target p has an integral c with Q_G(p−c)≤C_d/δ.",
      "hypotheses": "G is positive definite on a finite real coordinate set, with the full integer coordinate lattice. The dual quadratic bound holds for every nonzero integer covector.",
      "definitions": [
        "With first diagonal entry a and lower block D, the Schur complement is S=D−bbᵀ/a.",
        "The squared costs add after completing the square.",
        "C_d=1+8∑_{k=1}^d k² is an explicit witness for the existential constant."
      ],
