    {
      "id": "LTR-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The trace discriminant converts arithmetic and integer dual minima",
      "anchor": "inputs-transference-trace",
      "statement": "For a totally complex number field L of discriminant Δ and rank N, put d=N[L:ℚ]. Every archimedean target z has v∈𝒪_Lᴺ with q_h(z−v)≤C_d Δ²/(4 λ∨(h)).",
      "hypotheses": "N≥1, and the Hermitian matrix h_w is positive definite at each infinite place. There is one embedding representative per complex conjugate pair. The arithmetic dual uses the transposes of the inverse Hermitian matrices and the integral lattice.",
      "definitions": [
        "The integral trace matrix T of an integral basis has determinant Δ and adj(T)T=ΔI.",
        "Multiplying an integral covector by the trace adjugate produces a nonzero integral vector f.",
        "λ∨(h) is the minimum of the arithmetic dual squared length over nonzero integral vectors."
      ],
